fine, though, since there will obviously be background changes to supply a different setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-09-2018, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T03:03:33-07:00","id":1233373,"title":"","content":"Uhhh there are no Illithids... we call them Chulorviah...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T10:31:26-07:00","id":1233749,"title":"","content":"Fair point<br /> <br /> would Illithid work for a Beast concept? <br /> <br /> terrible Inscrutable, has mind power's, eats brains.... no idea what lessons it would teach... not sure I want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T10:56:13-07:00","id":1233757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1233359-illithid-the-flaying?p=1233749#post1233749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair point<br /> <br /> would Illithid work for a Beast concept?<br /> <br /> terrible Inscrutable, has mind power's, eats brains.... no idea what lessons it would teach... not sure I want to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> During the kickstarter with the first set of rules presented, I put together an illithid concept. It hinged a lot on the You Are Meat nightmare, which I don't think made it into the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I'm going to go easy this time: Mind Flayer. I could go a couple of different ways here. Makara makes sense because they live in the Underdark and have tentacles. However, I'm going to go with Namtaru. I find the idea of slimy tentacles sliding over my head and shoulders, questing for my brains to be pretty revolting. It also gives me access to their Birthright. Mind Flayer can inflict Confusion on its victim once per scene. (That's my way of translating some of their psychic power.)<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">What does a Mind Flayer hunger for? Braaaaaains! Well, yes, but what else do they do? They enslave beings in order to maintain the level of comfort they've become accustomed to. So, I'm giving this one a Hunger for Power. Ruling and dominating are bread and butter to the Mind Flayer.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">You Are Meat is a necessity for this Horror. Nothing is more delicious to it than when it gains another Thrall.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#020621\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Finally, a lesson. Originally, the lesson the Mind Flayer was supposed to teach was the power of collective action. Get enough people working for the same goal, and nothing is impossible. However, its Hunger has perverted the drive of the Mind Flayer. It would rather rule over everything than teach humanity anything.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T12:11:50-07:00","id":1235671,"title":"","content":"This is sort of a tangent but I was reading Antagonists and found an entry called &quot;The Hunger&quot;<br /> it turns you into a brain eating shark human.<br /> why not make flayers instead? just a hop and skip from shark to cephalopod<br /> <br /> I also think the Hunger is based on an episode of X-Files where there was a brain eating shark man and it played with the idea of addiction and recovery. Supernatural did the same thing with Rugaru but I think they transcribed one creatures lore to another creatures name...<br /> <br /> Tangeant complete. Maybe any of that is interesting or useful? Hammer the Hunger and its stages into a supernatural tolerance trait and clear path of evolution?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T23:42:29-07:00","id":1239578,"title":"","content":"Hm...could one make a non-profit fansplat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T00:58:52-07:00","id":1239597,"title":"","content":"Sure. WotC would stop Chronicles from making an Illithid game but I don't think they're going to mind if you make one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"",